        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: o cruzeiro",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "o cruzeiro — \"the cruise; the stone cross (by a road)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Os meus pais fizeram um cruzeiro de uma semana. My parents went on a week-long cruise."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In villages, um cruzeiro is a tall stone cross at a crossroads."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "cruzeiro is built on cruz 'cross', inherited from Latin crux, crucis (Lewis & Short); EtymDB lists Spanish crucero beside it. A cruise crosses the sea back and forth."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
